01a1026c-926c-729d-876f-2e038bbd7fce	\N	mcq	<p>The man was -------- for murder</p>	\N	<p>The correct sentence is:</p><p><strong>The man was hanged for murder.</strong></p><p>Here's why:</p><ul><li><p><strong>"Hanged"</strong> is the correct past participle of the verb "hang" when referring to execution by hanging.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Hanging"</strong> and <strong>"hung"</strong> are incorrect in this context.</p></li></ul><p>Therefore, "hanged" is the appropriate word to fill in the blank.</p><p>The correct answer is C because 'hanged' is the past tense when referring to execution by hanging. 'Hung' is used in other contexts.</p>	published	\N	70	2026-10-03 15:40:32.289159+00	2026-10-03 15:40:32.289159+00
