01a10253-0110-7545-9e97-293821fb095d	\N	mcq	<p>She is too tired to put _____ this noise anymore.</p>	\N	<p>Put up with- সহ্য করা।<br /><br />The correct phrase to complete the sentence "She is too tired to put _____ this noise anymore" is:</p><p><strong>up with</strong></p><p>Here's why:</p><ul><li><p><strong>"Put up with" is the most natural and idiomatic way to express tolerating something unpleasant, such as noise.</strong> It implies enduring or accepting something despite its negative aspects.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Put up at" is incorrect.</strong> It suggests staying or lodging somewhere, which doesn't make sense in this context.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Put on with" is also incorrect.</strong> It can have various meanings depending on the context, but none of them fit the idea of tolerating something unwanted.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Put on to" is grammatically incorrect and doesn't convey any meaningful sense in this situation.</strong></p></li></ul><p>Therefore, "She is too tired to put <strong>up with</strong> this noise anymore" accurately and idiomatically conveys the idea of her exhaustion and inability to tolerate the noise further.</p>	published	\N	11	2026-10-03 15:12:36.671946+00	2026-10-03 15:12:36.671946+00
