01a10264-59f7-76ab-b6bd-9e0d23ff5f27	\N	mcq	<p>Since the bus companies compete with one another, the drivers have every incentive to drive aggressively and take more passengers than the buses_____________ hold.</p>	\N	<p>In this sentence, the word "can" is used to express the capacity or ability of the buses. Let's break down the explanation with rules:</p><p>1. <strong>Modal Verb "Can":</strong> "Can" is a modal verb that is commonly used to indicate the ability or capacity to do something. In this context, it is used to convey the buses' capability or limitation.</p><p>2. <strong>Expressing Capacity:</strong> The sentence discusses the competitive environment among bus companies, and it suggests that due to this competition, the drivers are motivated to drive aggressively and take more passengers than the buses can physically hold.</p><p>3. <strong>Contextual Meaning:</strong> The use of "can" here implies a limitation on the number of passengers the buses are capable of accommodating. It highlights the practical or physical capacity of the buses.</p><p>In summary, the modal verb "can" is employed to convey the buses' limited capacity, and it fits well in the context of the sentence to describe the buses' inability to hold more passengers than their actual capacity.</p>	published	\N	30	2026-10-03 15:31:33.547773+00	2026-10-03 15:31:33.547773+00
