01a10298-e1ae-74c4-98c0-59dd69ba10cd	\N	mcq	<p>The police questioned each witness in ______.</p>	\N	<p>The most appropriate word to fill in the blank is <strong>turn</strong>. Here's why:</p><ul><li><p><strong>"Return"</strong> wouldn't make sense, as questioning each witness only happens once.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Order"</strong> could possibly work, but it's a bit awkward and generic. "Order" might imply specific order regarding importance or questioning sequence, which might not be intended.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Turn"</strong> is the most natural and idiomatic choice. It simply means that each witness had their turn to be questioned, indicating they were questioned one by one, individually.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Silence"</strong> doesn't directly relate to questioning each witness. It might only be relevant if silence was somehow enforced during the questioning.</p></li></ul><p>Therefore, <strong>"The police questioned each witness in turn"</strong> is the grammatically correct and most natural way to complete the sentence, clearly conveying the intended meaning.</p>	published	\N	133	2026-10-03 16:28:56.165523+00	2026-10-03 16:28:56.165523+00
