01a1029a-6c65-769a-97d5-425991b00e2c	\N	mcq	<p>Choose the correct verb form:</p><p>Once the peace accord had been signed, the guerrillas ____their arms.</p>	\N	<p>The correct verb form to complete the sentence is "laid down."</p><p>The complete sentence would be: "Once the peace accord had been signed, the guerrillas laid down their arms."</p><p>Explanation:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Laid down:</strong> This is the correct past participle form of the verb "lay down" in this context. It indicates the action of the guerrillas relinquishing or surrendering their arms after the peace accord.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lain down:</strong> This is not the correct form. "Lain" is the past participle of "lie" and is not appropriate in the context of putting down or surrendering arms.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lying down:</strong> This is a present participle phrase and does not fit the structure needed in this sentence.</p></li><li><p><strong>Laying down:</strong> This is a present participle phrase and is not the correct form for the past action described in the sentence.</p></li></ol><p>Therefore, the correct completion is: "Once the peace accord had been signed, the guerrillas laid down their arms."</p>	published	\N	7	2026-10-03 16:30:37.211594+00	2026-10-03 16:30:37.211594+00
