01a102e5-8a3b-768c-819d-1a24dd8fa570	\N	mcq	<p>I'll write down the phone number _____ I forget.</p>	\N	<p>The correct phrase to complete the sentence is "in case."</p><p>So, the sentence should be: "I'll write down the phone number in case I forget."</p><p>Explanation:</p><ul><li><p>"In case" is used when you do something as a precaution or because there is the possibility of something happening. In this sentence, writing down the phone number is a precaution against forgetting it.</p></li><li><p>"If" is used to introduce a conditional clause, typically indicating that something will happen if a particular condition is met. However, in this context, it doesn't fit because the action (writing down the phone number) is not conditional upon forgetting it, but rather a precaution against it.</p></li><li><p>"Unless" indicates a condition where something will happen only if another thing does not happen. It is not suitable in this sentence because the act of writing down the number is not contingent on not forgetting it.</p></li><li><p>"Even though" is used to introduce a statement that contrasts with something that has been mentioned. This doesn't apply here because there's no contrasting idea or situation.</p><p>ভুলে যেতে পারি এজন্য আমি ফোন নম্বরটি লিখে রাখব । এখানে শর্ত বোঝাচ্ছে না বলে if ব্যবহার না করে in case ব্যবহার করতে হবে ।</p></li></ul>	published	\N	55	2026-10-03 17:52:40.050108+00	2026-10-03 17:52:40.050108+00
