01a102ed-91fe-7407-ad86-d405b96c9974	\N	mcq	<p><span>Choose the correct sentence-</span></p>	\N	<p>Correct Answer</p><p>গ (We have a lot of work to do in summer)</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this context, "work" is an uncountable noun when referring to tasks or duties, so it should not be pluralized. The phrase "a lot of work" correctly conveys the idea of having many tasks to complete.</p><p>Analysis of Other Options</p><p>ক (We have many works to do in summer): This is incorrect because "works" typically refers to artistic or literary creations rather than tasks.</p><p>খ (We have much works to do in summer): This is incorrect because "much" is used with uncountable nouns, and "works" is not appropriate here.</p><p>ঘ (We have a lot of works to do in summer): This is also incorrect for the same reason as option ক; "works" should be singular in this context.</p>	published	\N	41	2026-10-03 18:01:26.330097+00	2026-10-03 18:01:26.330097+00
