01a102ef-597c-73ca-ae58-7d2b75360d2f	\N	mcq	<p>There are some qualities of a sonnet which make it different from other verse forms. Its definite restriction makes it a challenge to the artistry of the poet and call for all the technical skills at the poet's command. The more or less set rhyme patterns occurring regularly within the short space of fourteen lines afford a pleasant effect on the ear of the reader, and can create truly musical effects. The rigidity of the form precludes too great economy or to great prodigality of words. Emphasis is placed on exactness and perfection of expression. The brevity of form favors concentrated expression of ideas or passion. </p><p></p><p>The author's attitude towards the sonnet form can be best described as one of</p>	\N	Author সনেটের উপর জ্ঞানগর্ভ আলোচনা\r\nকরেছেন । আলোচনার মাধ্যমে তিনি কবিতা হিসেবে সনেটের\r\nপ্রশংসা করেছেন ।	published	\N	14	2026-10-03 18:03:22.936374+00	2026-10-03 18:03:22.936374+00
01a102ef-6599-7033-9c33-feadf4410a3d	\N	mcq	<p>Choose the correct sentence.</p>	\N	<p>The correct sentence is:</p><p>"The children were delighted by the monkeys swinging through the trees."</p><p>This sentence correctly uses the passive voice where the children (the subject) were delighted (the verb) by the monkeys swinging through the trees (the agent performing the action). It clearly conveys that the action of the monkeys swinging was the reason for the children's delight.</p><p>The other sentences are either awkwardly structured or grammatically incorrect:</p><ul><li><p>"Swinging of the monkeys through the trees, the children were delighted." This construction is awkward and does not clearly link the swinging of the monkeys to the children's delight.</p></li><li><p>"The monkeys swinging through the trees, the children were delighted." This sentence is a fragment. It lacks a clear connection between the two phrases and is missing a verb to link them.</p></li><li><p>"Because of monkey's swinging through the trees, the children were delighted." This sentence is almost correct but uses the possessive form 'monkey's' incorrectly. It should be 'monkeys' (plural) to indicate that multiple monkeys are swinging.</p></li></ul>	published	\N	16	2026-10-03 18:03:26.037917+00	2026-10-03 18:03:26.037917+00
