01a1030a-7482-711d-a273-a7c6139d0f2c	\N	mcq	<p>Choose the appropriate preposition: The\r\nambassador called ---- the President.</p>	\N	<p>1. <strong>Phrasal Verb "Call Upon"</strong>: In English, "call upon" is a phrasal verb that means to visit or request the presence or assistance of someone, especially in a formal or official capacity. This phrasal verb is often used in formal contexts, such as when someone in authority or prominence is being contacted or visited.</p><p>2. <strong>Appropriate Preposition</strong>: The choice of preposition after the verb "called" depends on the specific phrasal verb being used. In this case, the phrasal verb is "call upon," which is followed by the preposition "upon." </p><p>3. <strong>Meaning and Context</strong>: The preposition "upon" is used to indicate a close relationship or connection between the action of calling and the person being called. It suggests a sense of formality or respect, especially when contacting someone in authority or prominence, such as the President.</p><p>Given these rules and considerations, the appropriate preposition to use in the sentence "The ambassador called ___ the President" is "upon." Therefore, the correct sentence is: "The ambassador called upon the President."</p>	published	\N	67	2026-10-03 18:32:59.321951+00	2026-10-03 18:32:59.321951+00
