01a10311-c968-727a-8a23-9fc48a0002bc	\N	mcq	<p>Choose the correct option for the blank space. <br />After ______ threatened by the miscreants, he filed a case with the police.</p>	\N	<p>The correct option for the blank space is:</p><p><strong>having been</strong></p><p>Here's why:</p><ul><li><p><strong>"Being"</strong> is incorrect because it creates a dangling participle. The participle ("being threatened") requires a subject, but in this case, it comes after the main clause and doesn't clearly modify anything.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Having being"</strong> is redundant and grammatically incorrect. You only need one "having" with the past participle "been".</p></li><li><p><strong>"Been"</strong> is technically correct but sounds a bit terse and informal.</p></li><li><p><strong>"Having been"</strong> is the most grammatically correct and natural option. It smoothly connects the threat to the filing of the case, indicating that the threat happened before the case was filed.</p></li></ul><p>Therefore, "After <strong>having been</strong> threatened by the miscreants, he filed a case with the police" is the most appropriate and grammatically sound sentence.</p>	published	\N	42	2026-10-03 18:40:59.804701+00	2026-10-03 18:40:59.804701+00
