01a10319-8226-729a-809f-a5053cccf07b	\N	mcq	<p>Pinocchio is hungry and looks for an egg to cook ____ an omelet; but to his surprise, the omelet flies out of the window. </p><p>Choose the correct answer:</p>	\N	<p>নিজের কাজ নিজে করলে Reflexive pronoun (himself) হয়। এখানে Pinocchio নিজে ডিম ভাজি করেছিল, তাই Reflexive pronoun হিসেবে himself ব্যবহৃত হয়েছে।</p><p>The suitable word to fill in the blank for the sentence is “himself”.</p><p>Explanation:</p><ol><li><p><strong>His own self:</strong> This phrase is less common and may sound somewhat archaic. In modern usage, "himself" is more appropriate.</p></li><li><p><strong>Itself:</strong> This pronoun refers to a non-human or inanimate thing, and it doesn't convey the intended meaning in this context where Pinocchio is cooking.</p></li><li><p><strong>Oneself:</strong> While correct grammatically, "oneself" is a more formal or literary choice. In everyday language, "himself" is more commonly used in this context.</p></li><li><p><strong>Himself:</strong> This is the correct choice. It refers to Pinocchio and is used reflexively to indicate that he is cooking the omelet for himself.</p></li></ol>	published	\N	32	2026-10-03 18:49:25.852271+00	2026-10-03 18:49:25.852271+00
