01a1031f-200d-733a-8069-088730e9467b	\N	mcq	<p>A day on mars ____<strong> </strong>slightly ____<em> </em>than a day on earth.</p>	\N	<p>বাক্যটি Universal truth Present হওয়ায় present form-এ হবে । বাক্যে Than থাকায় তার পূর্বে Comparative form (longer) করতে হবে।</p><p>The correct sentence is: "A day on Mars is slightly longer than a day on Earth." </p><p>Explanation: "Is": The verb "is" is used to indicate a present tense statement. In this case, it is used to state a fact about the duration of a day on Mars compared to a day on Earth. </p><p>"Longer": The adverb "longer" is used to compare the lengths of the two days. It provides information about the comparative duration, indicating that a day on Mars has a greater length than a day on Earth. So, the complete sentence is comparing the lengths of days on Mars and Earth, stating that a day on Mars is slightly longer than a day on Earth.</p>	published	\N	87	2026-10-03 18:55:33.959008+00	2026-10-03 18:55:33.959008+00
