01a1031f-8eab-710d-830a-3876505102ed	\N	written	<p><span>Write a paragraph on <strong>"National Tourism and the COVID-19 Outbreak"</strong> by recalling the relevant unit from your textbook. <strong>"National Tourism and the COVID-19 Outbreak"</strong></span></p>	\N	<p><span>Covid-19 (Corona Virus disease) is an infectious disease caused by the SARS-COV-2 Virus. It was first identified in Chaina on 31 December 2019 &amp; in BD on 8th March 2020. Still now, this pandemic situation has not gone wholly. For this dangerous disease, Bangladesh has faced much difficult situation. Many sectors of BD have been damaged for this disease. One of the most flourishing sectors of Bangladesh is tourism industry. Our National Tourism industry has been hampered a lot for this pandemic situation. Some many important tourist places such as Kuakata (the Sagar Kannya), Sundarbans (the largest mangrove forest in the world), Cox's Bazar, (The world's biggest sea beach) are being damaged through this pandemic situation. The Covid-19 has several negative impacts on the tourism industry including the noticeable losses of revenue, a huge number of cuts off of jobs and closing the operation of businesses both permanently &amp; temporarily. For the Covid-19 Outbreak, the travellers &amp; tourists are also being deprived of getting natural elegance. It is totally impossible to get overcome this pandemic condition quickly but it is a matter of hope that our government has taken some strategies and for this our national tourism has begun to return to its former form. I think this industry will be able to add national revenue &amp; give pleasure to general people very soon</span></p>	published	\N	2	2026-10-03 18:56:02.270927+00	2026-10-03 18:56:02.270927+00
