01a10332-c315-70ca-88c8-5639e4f38d53	\N	mcq	<p>Find the correct sentences</p>	\N	<p>The correct sentences are:</p><p><strong>B. He nudged his companion.</strong></p><p><strong>C. He is to nudge his companion.</strong></p><p>Here's why:</p><ul><li><p><strong>A. He nudge his companion:</strong> This is grammatically incorrect. Verbs need to be conjugated to agree with the subject in number and tense. "Nudge" is the base form of the verb, while "he" requires the past tense form "nudged."</p></li><li><p><strong>B. He nudged his companion:</strong> This is grammatically correct and expresses a past action of nudging the companion.</p></li><li><p><strong>C. He is to nudge his companion:</strong> This is also grammatically correct and expresses a future instruction or expectation for the person to nudge his companion.</p></li></ul><p>Therefore, both B and C are correct sentences depending on the intended meaning: past action vs. future instruction.</p>	published	\N	2	2026-10-03 19:17:00.878508+00	2026-10-03 19:17:00.878508+00
