01a10337-1c72-7560-9d01-63c42092bc95	\N	mcq	<p>Rahim did not get admission because he _____.</p>	\N	<ul><li><p>Past Perfect Tense: "Had not studied enough" is in the past perfect tense, which is formed by using "had" plus the past participle "studied." This tense is employed to indicate that one action (not getting admission) was completed before another past action (the insufficient study efforts).</p></li><li><p>Emphasis on Antecedent Action: The use of past perfect often serves to highlight the completion of an action before another event in the past. In this case, the emphasis is on Rahim's failure to get admission, and the insufficient study is presented as the antecedent or prior action that contributed to this outcome.</p></li><li><p>Causal Relationship: By using the past perfect, the sentence makes it clear that the lack of admission is directly tied to Rahim's not having studied enough. It provides a clear cause-and-effect relationship between the two events.</p></li></ul><p>এখানে tense এর serial খেয়াল করতে হবে। রহিম admission নিতে পারেনি কারণ সে পড়াশুনা করেনি পড়াশুনা যেহেতু admission এর আগে করতে হয়, অতএব tense ও একধাপ পিছিয়ে যাবে। admission নেওয়া কথাটি past indefinite tense এ আছে, সেক্ষেত্রে পড়াশুনা করা কথাটি past perfect tense এ হবে।</p>	published	\N	61	2026-10-03 19:21:45.897653+00	2026-10-03 19:21:45.897653+00
