01a10352-2c0c-70e4-966b-65dc8ce04404	\N	mcq	<p>Mankind must develop a concern for wildlife creatures ___ save themselves. Choose the correct answer:</p>	\N	<p>The correct preposition to complete the sentence is "to."</p><p>The sentence with the correct preposition is:</p><p>"Mankind must develop a concern for wildlife creatures to save themselves."</p><p>Here's why "to" is the appropriate choice:</p><ul><li><p>In this context, "to" is used to indicate the purpose or reason for the action. The phrase suggests that in order for mankind to save themselves. They must develop a concern for wildlife creatures. The word "to" effectively links the need for concern for wildlife with the goal of self-preservation.</p></li></ul><p>The other options ("for," "of," "despite") do not correctly convey this relationship of purpose or reason in the sentence.</p>	published	\N	63	2026-10-03 19:51:19.357504+00	2026-10-03 19:51:19.357504+00
